# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# P2.3 — pointing the app at its Supabase project.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.real          then  bun run dev:real
#
# ★ THE FILE IS CALLED `.env.real`, NOT `.env`, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING.
#   Vite auto-loads `.env` and `.env.local` in EVERY mode. A `.env` sitting in
#   this repo would silently turn `bun run dev` into a real build — and then
#   `accept`, `outreach`, `rtl`, `mapfirst`, `splitter`, `touch`, `wizard`,
#   `import`, `layout` and `screenshots` would all open on a login form and
#   fail with two hundred confusing errors instead of one clear one.
#   `.env.real` is only read by `--mode real`, so demo mode stays the default
#   and the gates keep working exactly as they did before P2.3.
#
# BOTH VALUES ARE PUBLIC BY DESIGN and are meant to ship in the bundle: the
# publishable key NAMES the project, it authorises nothing. The security is the
# row-level security applied in P2.2 — which is why `bun run auth` proves that
# an anonymous read is REFUSED rather than proving that the key is secret.
#
# THE SERVICE-ROLE KEY IS NEVER FETCHED, NEVER COMMITTED AND NEVER REACHES THE
# CLIENT. If a step seems to need it in the browser, that step is wrong.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://lvrptqmkjikkkhcxocbe.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
